# Names only, never values (A15). Secrets live in the deployment's secret
# store and reach the app as environment variables.
#
# PHASE 1 NEEDS NONE OF THESE. The demo runs entirely in the browser: there is
# no backend, no database, and nothing to keep secret. This file exists so the
# shape is agreed before Phase 2 rather than invented under time pressure.

# ---- Phase 2: Supabase --------------------------------------------------
# THREE variables, and all three have to be set. The two keys are *something
# to choose*; the flag is *somebody choosing*. `isRealApi()` requires both
# conditions, deliberately — demo mode is a mode, never a fallback for a
# deployment that is missing a key, because a business booking real money
# against fixtures has no way to find out (src/lib/supabase/env.ts).
#
# Setting only the two keys leaves the app in demo mode with no error and no
# warning, which cost an afternoon on 2026-09-18. The flag is the one that
# decides.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_SUPABASE=1
#
# Publishable, safe in the browser.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# Server only. NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, never used in a request a user
# triggered — system jobs only (ADR-002).
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---- Phase 2: per-service base URLs -------------------------------------
# Each service is separately addressable. Moving one to its own host is
# changing one of these lines and nothing else (ADR-001).
# SERVICE_URL_IDENTITY=/api/v1/identity
# SERVICE_URL_PROCUREMENT=/api/v1/procurement
# SERVICE_URL_ACCOUNTING=/api/v1/accounting
# SERVICE_URL_DOCUMENTS=/api/v1/documents
# SERVICE_URL_EVENTS=/api/v1/events

# ---- Phase 2: outbox delivery -------------------------------------------
# OUTBOX_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---- Phase 2: Google Drive, for uploaded documents ----------------------
# Raw files go to an `ops` folder inside each module's shared drive (owner,
# 2026-09-21); metadata stays in Supabase. `/api/documents/upload` is the only
# server route in this application, and it exists solely because these two must
# never reach a browser.
#
# **Runtime secrets on the Worker** — Settings → Variables and Secrets. NOT
# Build variables: those are for `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values that get inlined into
# the client bundle, which is the one thing that must not happen to a key.
#
# `src/lib/drive.ts` refuses a NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed private key outright
# rather than reading it, the same way `serviceRoleKey()` does.
#
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=
# GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
#
# The folder ids themselves are NOT here: they live in
# `ops_core.drive_folders`, because IT changes them without a deploy and
# `ops_core.v_drive_readiness` reports which are still unset.
